<Legal
  lang="en"
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn how Tanukonomy handles your data today, and what's planned for accounts, sync, a premium plan, and usage analytics."
>
  <p class="lede">
    <strong>In short:</strong> Today, Tanukonomy does not collect or send your personal data to any server — everything
    you record stays on your device. We're working on an optional account (with sync and a premium plan) and basic usage
    analytics; both are covered in §6 and §7, will be announced transparently, and this policy will be updated before
    they go live.
  </p>

  <p>
    This policy explains how the Tanukonomy app (“the app”) and the tanukonomy.app website (“the site”) handle information.
    “We” means the developer of Tanukonomy.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data you record in the app</h2>
  <p>
    The app stores the data you enter yourself: wallets and balances, transactions (amount, date, category, note), budgets,
    freelance projects and hours, and app settings. This data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>is stored <strong>only in your device’s local storage</strong>;</li>
    <li>is never sent to our servers or third parties, because the app has no server;</li>
    <li>cannot be viewed, restored, or deleted remotely by us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What we currently don’t collect</h2>
  <p>
    This section describes things <strong>as they stand today</strong>. Some of it will change once the account,
    premium plan, and usage analytics features in §6 and §7 go live — neither is available yet.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>There is no account yet, so we don’t ask for your name, email, or phone number.</li>
    <li>There is no connection to banks, e-wallets, or payment services, and we never ask for passwords.</li>
    <li>There are no third-party analytics or ad trackers in the app. We don’t sell or share your data with advertisers,
      now or after §7 goes live.</li>
    <li>There is no access to your location, contacts, camera, or microphone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Because your data lives only on your device, you are fully in control. Uninstalling the app, or clearing its data in
    Android settings, permanently deletes all records. We keep no copy, so deleted data cannot be recovered by us.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Device backups</h2>
  <p>
    If your operating system’s built-in backup (such as Google backup on Android) is turned on, the system may include app
    data in your backup. Those backups are managed by the operating system provider under their policies, not by us.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Closed beta</h2>
  <p>
    To join the closed beta, you join a Google Group and the Google Play testing program with your Google account. Both are
    run by Google. As the group manager, we can see members’ email addresses; we use them only to grant beta access and do
    not share them. Feedback you send by email or through Google Play is used only to improve the app.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Coming feature: accounts, sync, and a premium plan</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to add accounts, so you can sync your data across more than one phone and unlock an optional premium plan
    (freemium). This feature is <strong>not available yet</strong>. A few things are already settled for when it ships:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>creating an account will be <strong>optional</strong> — core recording will keep working without one, fully
      offline as it does today;</li>
    <li>turning on sync will mean some data (wallets, transactions, budgets) is sent to a server to sync between your own
      devices, not shared with other users;</li>
    <li>a premium plan will need payment details; those are handled by a third-party payment provider (e.g. Google Play
      Billing), not stored by us directly;</li>
    <li>before accounts are active for anyone, we’ll update this policy with the full details: which server is used, how
      the data is protected, and how to delete your account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Coming feature: product usage analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to add basic analytics to understand how the app is used (e.g. which features get opened, where people get
    stuck) so we can improve it. This feature is <strong>not available yet</strong>. Its limits:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>it’s for <strong>product improvement</strong>, not for selling data or showing ads — Tanukonomy doesn’t show
      ads;</li>
    <li>it won’t include the content of your financial records (amounts, wallet names, transaction notes) — only feature
      usage patterns;</li>
    <li>before it goes live, we’ll name the analytics provider in this policy and give a way to opt out where the
      provider makes that available.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. This site</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses no cookies, forms, or analytics. The hosting provider may log standard technical data such as IP address
    and browser type for security and operations, under their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>The app is not directed at children under 13 and does not collect data from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If the app later adds a feature that changes how data is handled (including accounts, sync, the premium plan, and
    usage analytics in §6 and §7), we will update this page and its effective date before that feature becomes
    available.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
